<div class="pgs-wrap pgs-pdr">

  <div class="pgs-hero">
    <p class="pgs-eyebrow">Product Guide</p>
    <h1 class="pgs-heading">Everything you need to know.</h1>
    <p class="pgs-subhead">A thorough look at what DeskPaws is, how it works, and whether it&rsquo;s right for you and your cat.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="pgs-content pdr-content">

    <div class="pdr-intro">
      <p class="pdr-intro__text">Most cat owners who work from home have the same problem: their cat wants to be near them, and the only available surface is the desk. The keyboard, the notebook, the warm patch of sunlight next to the laptop. It&rsquo;s not mischief. It&rsquo;s proximity-seeking &mdash; cats prefer to be where you are.</p>
      <p class="pdr-intro__text">DeskPaws is built around that instinct rather than against it. Instead of blocking your cat or closing the door, you give them a designated spot within arm&rsquo;s reach &mdash; attached directly to your desk.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="pdr-section">
      <span class="pdr-section__marker">01</span>
      <div class="pdr-section__body">
        <h2 class="pdr-section__heading">What it is</h2>
        <p class="pdr-section__text">DeskPaws is a padded basket that clamps onto the edge of your desk. It hangs off one side &mdash; leaving your full desk surface clear &mdash; and creates a stable, dedicated perch for your cat at exactly the height they prefer: eye level with you.</p>
        <p class="pdr-section__text">The basket is lined with a removable sherpa-style insert. The clamp mechanism is adjustable and fits most desk thicknesses from one inch to four inches. No drilling, no adhesives, no permanent changes to your furniture.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="pdr-section">
      <span class="pdr-section__marker">02</span>
      <div class="pdr-section__body">
        <h2 class="pdr-section__heading">How the clamp works</h2>
        <p class="pdr-section__text">The mounting system uses a two-point clamping mechanism with wide rubber-coated contact pads that distribute weight evenly. There are no sharp edges that could mark a desk surface, and the clamp tightens with a single hand-turn knob &mdash; no tools required.</p>
        <p class="pdr-section__text">Once clamped, the connection is solid. The basket doesn&rsquo;t rock or shift under normal cat movement, including jumping in and out.</p>
        <div class="pdr-specs">
          <div class="pdr-spec">
            <span class="pdr-spec__label">Desk thickness</span>
            <span class="pdr-spec__value">1&Prime; &ndash; 4&Prime; (25 &ndash; 100&thinsp;mm)</span>
          </div>
          <div class="pdr-spec">
            <span class="pdr-spec__label">Max load</span>
            <span class="pdr-spec__value">Up to 50&thinsp;lbs (22.7&thinsp;kg)</span>
          </div>
          <div class="pdr-spec">
            <span class="pdr-spec__label">Installation</span>
            <span class="pdr-spec__value">No tools required</span>
          </div>
          <div class="pdr-spec">
            <span class="pdr-spec__label">Surface protection</span>
            <span class="pdr-spec__value">Rubber-coated contact pads</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="pdr-section">
      <span class="pdr-section__marker">03</span>
      <div class="pdr-section__body">
        <h2 class="pdr-section__heading">The basket and liner</h2>
        <p class="pdr-section__text">The basket is deep enough that cats feel enclosed on three sides &mdash; which matters, because cats sleep better in contained spaces. The walls come up high enough to create that sheltered feeling without blocking sightlines entirely.</p>
        <p class="pdr-section__text">Inside sits a thick removable sherpa liner. It lifts out for machine washing, and the basket itself wipes clean. Sherpa mimics the texture of soft fur, which is why most cats gravitate toward it almost immediately, without any special training.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="pdr-section">
      <span class="pdr-section__marker">04</span>
      <div class="pdr-section__body">
        <h2 class="pdr-section__heading">Will my cat actually use it?</h2>
        <p class="pdr-section__text">The honest answer: most do, and fairly quickly. Cats are drawn to elevated surfaces near their owners, and DeskPaws satisfies both conditions at once &mdash; it&rsquo;s high up, it&rsquo;s soft, and you&rsquo;re right there.</p>
        <p class="pdr-section__text">A light dusting of catnip on the liner on day one tends to accelerate adoption significantly. After the first few uses, the basket acquires the cat&rsquo;s own scent, and it becomes their space &mdash; one they return to on their own.</p>
        <p class="pdr-section__text pdr-section__text--note">For cats that take longer to accept new objects: placing a worn piece of clothing in the basket for a few days has worked well for many customers. Patience is the main ingredient.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="pdr-section">
      <span class="pdr-section__marker">05</span>
      <div class="pdr-section__body">
        <h2 class="pdr-section__heading">Who it&rsquo;s for</h2>
        <ul class="pdr-list">
          <li class="pdr-list__item">People who work from home with a desk-curious cat</li>
          <li class="pdr-list__item">Anyone whose cat has claimed the keyboard, mouse pad, or notebook</li>
          <li class="pdr-list__item">Cat owners who feel guilty isolating their cat during work hours</li>
          <li class="pdr-list__item">People looking for a considered gift for a cat-owning remote worker</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="pdr-section__text pdr-section__text--note">It works best for cats that are already desk-curious &mdash; those that jump up without being invited. If your cat actively prefers staying on the floor or in other rooms, a desk bed may not be the right fit.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="pdr-section">
      <span class="pdr-section__marker">06</span>
      <div class="pdr-section__body">
        <h2 class="pdr-section__heading">Setup in three steps</h2>
        <ol class="pdr-steps">
          <li class="pdr-step">
            <span class="pdr-step__num">1</span>
            <div class="pdr-step__body">
              <p class="pdr-step__label">Clamp it onto the desk edge</p>
              <p class="pdr-step__text">Position the basket where your cat tends to land. Tighten the knob by hand until secure. Takes about thirty seconds.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="pdr-step">
            <span class="pdr-step__num">2</span>
            <div class="pdr-step__body">
              <p class="pdr-step__label">Add a pinch of catnip to the liner</p>
              <p class="pdr-step__text">A small amount on day one helps introduce them to the space. After the first few visits, it&rsquo;s no longer necessary.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="pdr-step">
            <span class="pdr-step__num">3</span>
            <div class="pdr-step__body">
              <p class="pdr-step__label">Let them discover it</p>
              <p class="pdr-step__text">Most cats find it within the first hour. Sit at your desk and work normally &mdash; curiosity will do the rest.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>

  <div class="pdr-guarantee">
    <p class="pdr-guarantee__label">30-day guarantee</p>
    <p class="pdr-guarantee__text">We offer a 30-day return policy. If your cat genuinely won&rsquo;t use it after a fair try, contact us and we&rsquo;ll make it right. No restocking fees. No complicated process.</p>
